  "illustration_prompt": "Create a single publication-quality landscape 3:2 narrative illustration for an adult illustrated English-reading booklet. Finished standalone artwork, not a book mockup, not a collage of multiple unrelated panels. Sophisticated contemporary editorial gouache and watercolor, carefully controlled colored-pencil accents, velvety matte paint, subtle warm paper texture, soft natural daylight. Warm ivory paper dominates; subdued eucalyptus and sage greens structure the composition; restrained buttery lemon-yellow and dusty terracotta accents. Calm, comfortable, refined, credible drawing and natural anatomy. An airy coherent composition with one clear story focal point and at most two supporting details, generous breathing room at all edges and softly feathered painted edges into ivory. Detailed but uncluttered. Historically and scientifically appropriate objects, clothing and setting. Show the particular article's pivotal event or mechanism rather than a generic portrait or generic textbook symbols. Human figures treated with dignity; no grotesque caricature, no sensational violence or visible injuries. For disasters, emphasize the setting, evidence or human response without graphic suffering. For uncertain scientific claims, depict the observations and investigation without presenting debated mechanisms as proven. Absolutely no typography, captions, letters, numbers, logos, watermarks, diagram labels, fake writing or invented charts anywhere. Do not render invisible forces as literal magic. Avoid corporate vector icons, slick 3D rendering and childish cartoon style. High-quality, print-ready visual storytelling, matching a warm ivory-and-sage adult watercolor booklet.\n\nARTICLE-SPECIFIC SCENE: An intimate British family reading scene in the mid-1990s: an eight-year-old girl, Alice, seated comfortably beside a sage armchair, absorbed in the first chapter of a plain unlettered manuscript. She looks eagerly toward her father, a modestly dressed publisher in an ordinary sweater, who is handing her a few more blank manuscript pages. Her delighted appetite for the next chapter is the focal event; do not portray J.K. Rowling, Hogwarts, a wizard, a book cover or magical effects. No corporate identity, no rejection letters with fabricated writing. Natural faces and hands, a believable small family sitting room, a little daylight and restrained terracotta upholstery, generous warm ivory breathing room. Manuscript pages show only paper texture with no typography.",
